      "problem": "Factor ${h}^{4}-10{h}^{2}+25.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can introduce a new variable $z={h}^{2}$ and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{4}-10{h}^{2}+25 & ={({h}^{2})}^{2}-10({h}^{2})+25 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-10z+25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic as the square of a sum, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of $h:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-10z+25 & ={(z-5)}^{2} \\\\  & ={({h}^{2}-5)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
